WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.860
SPACE FLEET BATTLE

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.660
"Space Fleet Battle".
SPACE FLEET BATTLE

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.530
Any armor that's cracked, get it welded!

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.400
Don't make it sound so easy!

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:33.030
Is that any way for a soldier to talk?!

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.830
What? This is a military force?!

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.860
Raise levels three and five a bit more!

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.560
Wait a second, please!

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.830
Hey! Haven't you contacted Marbet, yet?

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.600
Looks like the oxygen tanks still have some use.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.360
Thank goodness.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:08.400
I know this solar battery's big, but it's about 300 square kilometers?!

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:11.630
15 kilometers wide and 120 kilometers long.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.960
I've finished painting the chest.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.460
I guess that'll do.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.960
Karel, thanks for the help.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.160
You're welcome.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:18.930
Üso!

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.560
Is it done, Tomáš?

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.760
I connected a compressed gas controller to his computer.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.060
Try calling him.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.500
Haro, come!

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.430
Haro!

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.330
Üso!

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.600
You need to change the tanks pretty often, though.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.900
I have a wire! Haro!

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.800
Ow! I hit! Ow! Ow!

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.800
Üso, pull!

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:44.500
Thanks.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.330
No prob.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.730
So, the Hiland's energy covers the Asian region?

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.600
We don't send it now.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:51.430
Why not?

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.430
The Earth Federation Government probably stopped it because...

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:57.100
...they're thinking about when Earth is taken by the Zanscare Empire.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.260
Really?

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:01.230
The PCST hasn't sent a ship in a year.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.260
They've pretty much cut us loose.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.830
The Reineforce is en route.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:10.660
Üso!

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.460
Yes?

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.960
Did you change the Zoloat's IFF code to the League Militaire's?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.460
Yes, I finished with that.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.760
Is the enemy coming?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.200
You think they won't?

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.260
Understood.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.530
Ms. Elisha!

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.700
Haro! Haro!

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.200
Marbet! Haro! Marbet!

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.900
Quit blocking the camera!

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.300
I can't see the construction block if you're in the way, right?

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.560
Ha-Haro!

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:33.330
Right.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.230
Is BESPA coming?

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.930
No. Not right away,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.900
but there's a good chance they will, so...

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.160
We drove off the Bagley Team,

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.560
so now Federation ships are coming directly from Earth?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.930
From the silhouette, we've determined it's the Reineforce.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.360
It's 50 years old. I'm surprised it made it up here.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:07.260
We've begun docking all the pieces of Keilas Guilie together.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.000
One Amalthea-class and two Sinopes. That's all we can send?

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.460
More than enough to see what the Federation is up to.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.360
Godwald, you still need your rest.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.060
Sir.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.330
And I'd like to see Lt. Cronicle's skills.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.900
Estimating from its orbit,

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:42.500
the Reinforce must have also launched from Arti Gibraltar.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.600
So, the League Militaire and...

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.060
the Federation Forces are both making their move.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.930
Is this the one, Tomáš?

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:49.730
Thanks.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.430
Sorry.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:54.630
No prob. We took the Aeneus out for a test drive three days ago.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.630
Still, I'm amazed you built this rocket to get home.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.800
A vain struggle for survival.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.360
Martina! Where are you? Give me a hand!

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.860
Um, I can help!

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.330
What's that?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.260
Hey, hold it!

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:11.200
Something's not right.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.500
Looks that way.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.830
Stop all ship repairs!

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.960
All hands, level one battle stations!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.600
Mobile suits, once you're ready to launch,

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.000
cover the Reineforce's forward airspace!

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.700
Oliver, we put a hornless head on your unit.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.600
Thanks! Now stand back!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.200
Kuffu, clear the mechanics from the suits!

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.930
Units 2 and 3, okay!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.460
It's up to you, Miss Junko!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.630
Thanks!

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.560
Peggie, Cony, you ready?

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.700
Did you hear that, Miss Juca?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.000
We're not used to space, so we'll be needing you.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.300
What's wrong?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.330
Are you catching a cold?

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:53.830
I'm just a little dizzy.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:57.200
Martina, take some medicine for your fever.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.360
You should do what your sister says, Martina.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.300
That girl is hopeless...

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.630
I've been wondering, why did BESPA take her and the others before?

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:13.330
Probably to force them to turn the Hiland horizontally and send them electricity, right?

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.930
I'm asking if she heard what their plans are!

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:22.960
I know the direction they ordered us to turn has a BESPA ship called Keilas Guilie,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.730
but I don't know what their plans are.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.530
It was for Keilas Guilie!

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.260
Elisha! Elisha! Elisha!

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.260
Üso, we're going out to meet the Reineforce.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.260
Reineforce?

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.800
It's a League Militaire ship that Lt. Gomez and the old men procured.

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:40.630
They're all headed here?

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.700
Everyone, prep for depressurization!

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:44.900
What's up?

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.600
We're sending out both mobile suits.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:47.600
Both?

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.060
Have we contacted the battleship Gaunland yet?

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.060
Not yet, why?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:02.660
No reason, but Jinn Jahannam is aboard the Gaunland, right?

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.330
Yeah.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.230
Well, the leader of the League Militaire goes so many places.

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.600
It's great, right?

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.000
He wants to ask about his parents...

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.760
Opening the construction block hatch!

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.400
Üso, here we go.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:22.700
Right!

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.100
Once the Zoloats launch, perhaps we should bring...

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:39.330
...the two Sinopes in to cover our right and left, Captain.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.660
Right. We're just facing a single old battleship. We should have no trouble.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:47.500
The Reineforce may be alone, but don't underestimate it, Captain.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.130
Is there something bothering you?

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:50.730
No.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:57.230
Commander Oliver, you guard the Reineforce with your one suit.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.160
Roger.

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:08.930
Disperse Minovsky particles at combat density!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.400
Bridge, move to battle position!

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:17.760
Come on!

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.730
Get in, or you'll die!

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.730
Okay, that should do it.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:26.300
Suzy, I'll check your backpack.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.260
Isn't it kind of soon to shut the visor?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.260
He'll get out, otherwise.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:32.530
True...

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:35.330
How much oxygen does a dog use?

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.000
Fireballs? Did they find the Reineforce?

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.300
What?!

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.400
The captured Sinope?

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.500
Tomáš came out here on his own?

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:58.460
Üso, send them back!

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.100
R-Right!

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.130
This is gonna turn into a real battle!

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.800
We brought you spare weapons.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.430
This is too dangerous for kids!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:16.560
I'm older than you, Üso! And you need the support.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.430
That may be true, but... But, Tomáš!

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:28.030
Warren!

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.260
You don't have time to come in here!

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:30.900
But...

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:35.530
Never mind that... What do you do when you like a girl?

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:36.760
A girl?

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.830
You like Shahkti, right?

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.600
Like a little sister...

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.800
And Miss Katejina?

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:43.960
And Miss Marbet?

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:50.900
Üso, you've read all sorts of books!

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.230
What do they say?

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.160
Odelo! Tomáš! Please, everyone, go back.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:59.900
You can just leave the spare weapons floating around here.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.400
Üso, help me out here!

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.800
In novels, you give them jewelry and stuff on their birthday!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.560
That's not happening!

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.230
Lemme go!

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.460
How about flowers?!

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.660
Flowers?

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:18.600
Yeah, flowers...

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.200
A girl he likes, huh?

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.700
I wonder if she made it into space, too?

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:37.230
Üso, we're entering the Minovsky particle region.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:40.230
We're going to lose radio comms, okay?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:41.930
R-Right!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.660
I'm tying us all together. Just hang on for a while.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:54.260
Come on, don't cry.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.960
Send out Zoloat 6! Hurry!

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.030
Sorry to be selfish, Captain.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:24.260
It's okay. Just please give our advance suits some fighting spirit.

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:29.060
Cronicle, Unit 6, moving out!

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:38.160
Let's see how much trouble the League Militaire's old battleship gives us.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.330
A Victory-type's fighting!

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:53.030
But, there are three or four Victory-types on this ship, right?

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:55.230
Is it Oliver or Junko?

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:58.800
I can't see Shrike Team's Gun EZs!

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:02.200
That's Üso's Gundam!

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.830
How can you tell?

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.100
I just know!

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:12.030
Captain Gomez, Romero, Mr. Leonid! It's Marbet!

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.060
I'll cover you in this white Zoloat!

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.230
Marbet, you're alive!

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.260
I don't need a normal suit till things look dire. Ruins morale.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:25.600
Wires, huh?

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:26.860
Ridiculous!

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:34.060
Reineforce pilots!

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:37.900
I'll show you how to deal with the Zoloat's battle tactics!

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:51.730
Cony! Ready? We'll squeeze them!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.430
Except we're the ones getting squeezed!

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.400
Fall back to the Reineforce's airspace!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.000
There are still a bunch of enemy units!

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.600
That light is from wires!

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:22.300
You can't threaten us with nets!

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:27.030
You want a threat? Fine then!

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:32.160
There!

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.930
You're playing with me?!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.600
The League Militaire's white one! How dare it fly around so casually!

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:48.630
I won't let you catch me!

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.660
Should we be flying without cover fire?

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.000
We're still too far out.

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:57.630
Flowers...

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:03.560
One of ours?

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:04.900
Confused him!

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:07.830
I'm a friendly!

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:16.700
I'm not letting a kid and Shrike Team hog all the glory!

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:17.730
Next!

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.700
Found it! It looks like the Victory!

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.960
Fire the missiles!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.630
Just don't hit it directly!

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:28.660
Of course not!

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:33.330
Wait! The Minovsky particles are interfering with the camera's image.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:36.900
It's your job to read that, Karel!

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.100
We'll move closer.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:44.660
Okay, fire!

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:45.460
Right!

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:57.730
Another net!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.430
Trying to surround me?!

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.660
Hold it!

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.960
I saw one Zoloat attacking another!

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:14.260
Could I have seen it wrong? No!

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:15.830
I can do that, too!

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:22.700
Was I saved again?

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.160
Miss Peggie? Miss Cony?

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:29.760
Am I just no good at space and team combat?

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.200
You're mine!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.760
The Amalthea's getting careless with its positioning. Captain!

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:48.930
Our barrage is too thin! Take evasive action and return fire!

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.900
If we've given it all we have, this is pathetic!

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.200
Our evasive action's too slow!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:13.900
What are those beams?

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:16.200
Is that you, Gaunland? Do you read?

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:17.700
Roger!

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:22.400
Reinforcements have arrived for the Reineforce?!

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.160
Why didn't we notice them?!

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.630
Mobile suits also approaching!

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.930
Six of the Gaunland's Javelins, approaching from above to assist!

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:35.060
So, the League Militaire weren't lying to us.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.760
I guess Jinn Jahannam was...

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:39.900
...successful in getting some of the Earth Federation Space Force!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.330
Separating above and below? I'll stop you!

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:48.030
This will do it!

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:48.900
What?!

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.700
That little...

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:04.000
Reinforcements have arrived? Amalthea, can you retreat?

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:09.960
Have the Sinopes open suppressive fire from our flanks!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:10.700
Fall back!

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:11.500
Sir!

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:30.430
That solar battery is the only place in the area that the Reineforce can escape to.

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.800
It mustn't be damaged. Retreat!

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.430
Is Jinn Jahannam...

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.830
Is Mr. Jinn Jahannam on this ship?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.230
Turret number 3's taken heavy damage!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:23.530
Roger that!

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:25.500
Where's Mr. Jinn Jahannam?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:27.900
On the bridge. Wait, who are you?

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:29.200
Thank you!

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:39.330
What's that nurse doing?!

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:42.260
I got knocked around when we took a direct hit!

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.430
I might have a broken bone!

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:46.160
Don't manhandle me!

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:47.460
Pardon me.

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:50.400
Which one is Mr. Jinn Jahannam?

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:52.600
What are you doing here?

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:53.760
What took you?!

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:57.630
I beg your pardon, Your Excellency Jinn Jahannam!

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.060
Are you people trying to kill me?!

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:04.530
How would any of you know how much an injured man is suffering?!

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:07.230
That's Jinn Jahannam?

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:11.360
I'm still bleeding! Hurry up and stop the bleeding!

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:14.830
I don't understand. The leader of the League Militaire...

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:19.160
...that the count and Mr. Romero and Miss Marbet talked about is this man?

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.400
But, it's a fact that he brought...

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:27.800
...this Federation Forces ship to assist the Reineforce.

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:29.900
What's going on?

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.130
Understood. I'll get it ready.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:48.600
Good job out there.

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:50.930
You did a great job too, Miss Marbet.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.800
What's wrong? You went to the Gaunland, right?

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:54.630
Yeah.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:56.300
Was Jinn Jahannam there?

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:57.200
Yeah.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.300
He yelled a lot.

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:03.960
He's a busy man. He didn't tell you about your parents?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:07.000
No... But that's not all.

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:09.830
I understand. He's not what you hoped he'd be.

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:12.800
For example, did you think...

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.900
...that Jinn Jahannam might have been your father?

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.700
Don't be ridiculous!

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:21.830
I'd never have a childish fantasy like that!

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:24.900
I hate people like him!

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.800
Don't be angry, Üso.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.730
It's okay.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:33.900
Your father and mother are still alive.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:36.300
Doing great things.

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.300
Yeah. Yeah, they are.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:42.060
They must be.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.300
Yeah, I think so, too.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:48.200
Really?

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:53.330
Hey, you know Miss Marbet already has Mr. Oliver, right?

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:54.960
What kind of crazy thing is that to say?!

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:59.060
If you're gonna say that, then Elisha already has Tomáš!

00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:03.560
Dammit, Üso! You had to go and say it?!

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:05.400
Who made me say it?!

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:06.800
Listen, you!

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:08.230
What?!

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:10.960
Never mind!

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:12.560
Yeah.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.760
Martina! Martina!

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:19.230
Um, look, Martina...

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:20.300
What's up?

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:21.360
Um...

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:22.560
What is it?

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:24.960
Please accept these!

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:27.700
What are you doing with those?!

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:32.100
I tried my best to find flowers that suited you, Martina?

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:35.560
Don't you know what the flowers on the Hiland are for?!

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:38.230
These are invaluable for keeping the air clean,

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.030
and you picked some?!

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.560
I forgot!

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:47.930
Flowers grown on an artificial satellite are really important!

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:50.030
And I totally forgot!

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:52.560
I'll get this serviced aboard the Reineforce.

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:54.460
And I'll speed up the preparations here.

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:56.860
Warren's nice, don't you think?

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.730
Why do you think I made him my little brother?

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:00.360
See you.

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:01.000
Yeah.

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:39.630
Searching for us after we're thrown out into space,

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:45.530
Üso, Tomáš, and the others are attacked by BESPA's regular forces.

00:23:46.030 --> 00:23:50.500
And an unbelievable destiny befalls me.

00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:54.230
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

